  "markscheme": {
    "html": "<p>Correct answer: B</p>\n<p>A: Photon energy equals the magnitude of the energy-level difference, <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"E_\\gamma=|E_f-E_i|\"></span>. This transition has a smaller <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\Delta E\"></span> than transitions to <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"n=1\"></span>.</p>\n<p>B: For hydrogen, <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"E_n=-13.6\\,\\text{eV}/n^2\"></span>, so <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\Delta E=13.6\\,(1/1^2-1/4^2)=13.6\\,(1-1/16)=12.75\\,\\text{eV}\"></span>, the largest among the options.</p>\n<p>C: Photon energy equals the magnitude of the energy-level difference, <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"E_\\gamma=|E_f-E_i|\"></span>. This transition is between higher <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"n\"></span> levels, giving a relatively small <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\Delta E\"></span>.</p>\n<p>D: <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\Delta E=13.6\\,(1/1^2-1/2^2)=13.6\\,(1-1/4)=10.2\\,\\text{eV}\"></span>, which is less than the <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"n=4\"></span> to <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"n=1\"></span> transition.</p>"
  },
  "paper": "paper_1a",
  "question": {
    "html": "<p>Which of the following transitions in hydrogen will emit the photon with the greatest energy?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"n=3\"></span> to <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"n=2\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"B\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"n=4\"></span> to <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"n=1\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"C\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"n=5\"></span> to <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"n=3\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"D\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"n=2\"></span> to <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"n=1\"></span></p></li></ol>"
  },
